  "step_3": "The decision reason is about skewness — specifically, preferring a lottery that is more left-skewed (i.e., more probability on favorable outcomes). However, in this case, both lotteries have a small probability of a positive outcome (0.2% and 0.1%), and the rest is on 0 Euros, so both are right-skewed (mass on the left). Thus, neither is left-skewed, and the reason does not apply. The individual's reasoning focuses on the magnitude of the payoff (6000 > 3000) and the extremely low probability, suggesting a preference for the higher payoff, not on skewness. There is no mention of distribution shape or skewness in the report. Therefore, the individual did not use the decision reason about skewness. The reason is not applicable to the problem, and the reported reasoning is fundamentally different. Hence, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
